Z||000000||sid1200||07-07-99||09:42 PM||||hi anyone know where I can get a sunroof storage case and sunshade (also how does the sunshade attach)<br>and is it possible to store the roof under the hood (I think that is the proper loc) without the bag?<p>thanks<br>sid
Z||000001||Phil||07-08-99||04:55 AM||||I store my roof in the trunk without this bag I hear about all the time.
Z||000002||GREENDANO||07-08-99||06:27 PM||||Rodney Dickman had the bag you want, I don't know if it's still available.  <br>www.execpc.com/~rodney1/
Z||000003||sid1200||07-08-99||11:51 PM||||do u mean store in the front trunk or the back trunk?<p>and if the back, is there any  danger of the roof breaking on rough roads?<p>thanks
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||07-09-99||02:18 AM||||Sid1200, the Fiero comes with brackets under the hood above the spare tire to carry the sunroof. Also there is a spot underneath it to store the wind deflecter too. My 86(god rest it's sole) had this. I removed it and installed it in my 88(along with most of eveything else). The brackets are just plastic and will bolt in any Fiero. There are 2 small ones to the front of the compartment and 1 big one towards the rear. If you were to find these in the boneyard I don't think it would cost more than 20 bucks or so.<p>As far as the bag, I think they were aftermarket. My Fiero didn't have it and I have never seen one in person. And yes the sunroof fits without the bag.
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||07-09-99||04:40 AM||||Sid, take a look at the pictures below. The first pic shows how the sunroof is stored in the front compartment. The white arrows show where the protective rubber pads should be.<p>The second pic shows how the wind deflector is stored. Hope this helps.<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.pennock.nl/images/sunroof1.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.pennock.nl/images/sunroof2.jpg"> 
Z||000006||theogre||07-09-99||10:24 PM||||there are 2 threads you created on this topic, read both. None of us call the front a trunk. With the exception of the storage of the roof glass, and in my case a very small air pump(I hate paying repeatedly for compressed air.), there is no storage for anything besides the tire in the front.<p>I.E. Fiero's that came with factory roof glass also came with front compartment storage for the glass. Cliff's excelent images explain it all.
